tion 1 with the corresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nBefore going out to buy groceries, my mom told me to do the laundry, and I agreed. But after she left, I was too lazy to do it. Without realizing it, my mom suddenly called me from downstairs. Going downstairs, I thought I was in big trouble for not doing what she had asked me to do. She asked me whether I had done the laundry, and I averted her gaze while saying yes. Once my mom went to cook dinner, I immediately went upstairs to do the laundry.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would my mom ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Oblivious & Trust\nB) Trust & Delight\nC) Oblivious & Pride\nD) Embarrassment & Delight\nE) Caring & Delight\nF) Embarrassment & Caring\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would my mom feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) She thinks I did the laundry as she asked & She didn't know I lied\nB) She appreciates me doing the chores & She didn't see me come downstairs\nC) She didn't see me come downstairs & She is in a good mood before cooking dinner\nD) She appreciates me doing the chores & She didn't know I lied\nE) She thinks I did the laundry as she asked & She knows I didn't do the laundry as she asked\nF) She didn't know I lied & She didn't see me come downstairs","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.014055469740182189,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af5a6c29aa9dc5a833d9a39","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794483906041,"createTime":"2026-11-12 19:45:06","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"co